  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "v1.1.0 - 2026-11-25\n\nAdded\n- ICachedDatabentoClient, which CachedDatabentoClient implements: the time-series calls with a CacheMode, the\n  batch calls and the ArchiveFileUnreadable event, so code can be handed a fake in tests. An implementation\n  writes only the 11 async calls for several symbols; CachedDatabentoClientExtensions adds the one-symbol and\n  sync forms.\n- CachedDatabentoClient is an IDatabentoTimeseriesClient (client 2.7.0) and serves its calls from the cache\n  (CacheMode.Use), so code that takes either Databento client takes the cache too. The cache still refuses\n  ALL_SYMBOLS: it needs the raw symbols.\n\nChanged\n- Built on Databento.CSharpApiClient 2.7.0 (it was 2.6.0).\n\nv1.0.0 - 2026-11-24\n\nFirst release.\n- CachedDatabentoClient: the client's time-series calls for cbbo-1s, cbbo-1m, bbo-1s, bbo-1m, tcbbo, trades,\n  ohlcv-1s/1m/1h/1d and statistics, async and sync, served per symbol and UTC day from the cache, else\n  downloaded whole, and saved before the call returns once Databento says the day is final. JSON or DBN\n  transport, a Bypass mode that downloads again, and empty days saved only when symbology confirms the symbol\n  was not listed (by default).\n- Batch jobs for ranges too large for the time-series calls, with a cost cap and reuse of a job that already\n  covers the range; any Databento batch download folder can be ingested too.\n- DatabentoArchiveCompactor: folds day files into one Parquet archive per dataset, schema, group and month,\n  checked record by record (by default) before the files it replaces are deleted.\n- DatabentoCacheBackup and DatabentoCacheRestore: the whole cache as one checked tar in an IBackupStore, with\n  retention, a dry run, and a restore that refuses while the cache is in use.\n\nFull history: https://github.com/mrut2pac/Databento.CSharpApiClient.Caching/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md",
